  "summary": "Doable is a self-hosted, MIT-licensed, multi-tenant AI app builder with sandboxed code execution, RBAC/MFA/audit logging, a pnpm/Turborepo monorepo (Next.js web, Hono API/WS, PostgreSQL 16), BYOK provider support, and one-click deployment paths. Evidence is documentation-based; the community Code of Conduct defines an escalation ladder from private warning to permanent ban. Evidence coverage: 151 of 293 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
